I'm seeing the expert class fulminate over the Bessent Twist, which I can understand, but seems wiser to just assume the govt (regardless of party, see below) will intervene to keep markets how they want them. If you start from that place, you won't get outraged or even fazed by this stuff and it def makes it much easier to stay the course as long-term investor (which is most fruitful form of alpha IMO). A twofer.

I went even further in a note a month ago.. as I think we haven't seen nothing yet in terms of govt intervention in markets. Fast fwd 15yrs I think treasury is one of the biggest owners of equity ETFs a la Japan and China. https://t.co/lGgMsN8Exm

@sl_wire Right they don't own any eq ETFs now.. but they did buy a bunch of bond ETFs during COVID and seeing how well equity ETF purchases worked for China recently we think it will become another tool in their arsenal down road

@peasant_trader @LynAldenContact It is if you hold it long enough. Try comparing a 30yr $SPY holders returns to any pro HF, MF or otherwise

